(defrule registry -> registry-need registry-components registry-schema registry-dispatch registry-hooks registry-approval registry-approval-store changes)
(defrule registry-need -> :background registry-need/flat :nucleus registry-need/registry)
(defrule registry-need/flat -> :instruction "平らな名前空間に置くと管理できなくなる問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "A flat namespace of tools becomes unmanageable as capabilities grow: hard-coded dispatch logic is inflexible, and dynamic plugin loading without structure is unsafe.")
(defrule registry-need/registry -> :instruction "採った方式を 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev adopts a registry with handler categories, organizing tools into handler classes with schema-based registration.")
(defrule registry-components -> :instruction "道具の仕組みを分ける関心を 1 文で書く" :sample "The tool system separates schema construction, dispatch routing, and lifecycle hooks into distinct components.")
(defrule registry-schema -> :instruction "道具の定義を集める部品と、集める出どころを 1 文で書く" :sample "ToolSchemaBuilder assembles JSON schemas from three sources: (1) static _BUILTIN_TOOL_SCHEMAS defining approximately 40 built-in tools, with descriptions loaded from markdown templates via load_tool_description(); (2) dynamically discovered MCP schemas, including only those tools in the _discovered_mcp_tools set to avoid context bloat; and (3) subagent schemas injected by the SubAgentManager when present.")
(defrule registry-dispatch -> :instruction "呼び出しを取り扱い部品へ配る部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "ToolRegistry serves as the central dispatcher, mapping tool names to handler methods across 12 handler classes organized by category (file, process, web, notebook, user interaction, task management, thinking, MCP discovery, batch execution; see Table 1 in Appendix A for the complete mapping).")
(defrule registry-hooks -> :nucleus registry-hooks/extend :elaboration-set-member registry-hooks/pre :elaboration-object-attribute registry-hooks/external)
(defrule registry-hooks/extend -> :instruction "フックが取り扱い部品を変えずに拡張を可能にすることを 1 文で書く" :sample "Lifecycle hooks provide extensibility without modifying handler code.")
(defrule registry-hooks/pre -> :instruction "実行前のフックができることを 1 文で書く" :sample "PreToolUse hooks fire synchronously before execution: a hook returning exit code 2 hard-blocks the tool call, returning an error to the model that no amount of prompt engineering or approval configuration can override.")
(defrule registry-hooks/external -> :instruction "外部の手続きがフックとして受け取る情報と使い道を 1 文で書く" :sample "External scripts registered as hooks receive full event context as JSON on stdin (including session ID, working directory, tool name, tool input, and (for post-hooks) tool response), enabling project-specific policies such as blocking writes to protected paths, enforcing naming conventions, or streaming audit logs to external systems.")
(defrule registry-approval -> :nucleus registry-approval/gate :elaboration-part-whole registry-approval/levels :elaboration-general-specific registry-approval/danger)
(defrule registry-approval/gate -> :instruction "呼び出しが届く前に承認が門を置くことを 1 文で書く" :sample "Before any tool call reaches its handler, the runtime approval system gates execution based on user-configured trust boundaries.")
(defrule registry-approval/levels -> :instruction "自律の水準を 1 文で書く" :sample "Three autonomy levels control the default posture: Manual requires explicit approval for every tool call; Semi-Auto auto-approves read-only operations (a curated allowlist of commands such as ls, cat, git status) while prompting for writes; and Auto approves all operations for trusted workflows.")
(defrule registry-approval/danger -> :instruction "上書きできない危険の規則があれば書く" :sample "Default danger rules at priority 100 (matching patterns such as rm -rf /, rm -rf *, and chmod 777) are always active and cannot be overridden by user configuration or approval-level changes.")
(defrule registry-approval-store -> :nucleus registry-approval-store/stores :elaboration-object-attribute registry-approval-store/precedence)
(defrule registry-approval-store/stores -> :instruction "承認の規則を実行をまたいで残す保管先を 1 文で書く" :sample "Approval rules persist across sessions via two JSON stores: user-global rules at ˜ /.opendev/permissions.json and project-scoped rules at .opendev/permissions.json.")
(defrule registry-approval-store/precedence -> :instruction "保管先が複数あるときの優先を 1 文で書く" :sample "When both exist, project rules take priority for the same pattern, enabling per-repository trust boundaries (e.g., a shared project can restrict docker commands that a user’s personal config allows).")
(defrule changes -> :instruction "登録の仕組みが経た転換を、1 行に 1 つ、置き換えた設計の名前で挙げる" :frame "opendev.design-change.lisp")
